s from 1951 to 2025. On the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 6 grids, March to April came in under 90% of normal in 41 of those years. In 2026 so far, February to March sat at 8% of normal and March to April at 10% on the middle of the grids. Every grid had its driest year in 1956, with grid 20824 down at 43% of normal that year.</p>"}
